-5c8c-8baf-fe50f2bdfc52" :question/math-academy-id "q-102693" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in ${\\text{m/s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=3+8t-3{t}^{2}$, where $t$ is the time in seconds. If the particle has velocity $v=-1\\,\\text{m/s}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{s}$, calculate the speed of the particle at the moment $t=2\\,\\text{s}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (3+8t-3{t}^{2})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3t+4{t}^{2}-{t}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(0)=-1.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & =3(0)+4(0)^{2}-(0)^{3}+C \\\\ -1 & =0+C \\\\ C & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=3t+4{t}^{2}-{t}^{3}-1.$\n\nWe evaluate the velocity at time $t=2\\,\\text{s}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =3(2)+4(2)^{2}-(2)^{3}-1 \\\\  & =6+16-8-1 \\\\  & =13\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the speed is equal to $|v(t)|,$ we conclude that the speed of the particle is $13\\,\\text{m/s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-102693/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee2920dc-93e1-5595-a751-62ad5e4f3035"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102693"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81474/selection/41960dd54deb249b69963946aad073a9efdee28d29175fa0fb77c9989bed55c0" :answer/id #uuid "dfd80d09-4e56-593c-93b9-b51f7f9c1c28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81474/selection/65d8c559c809217f473c7ef19de0ff6b5a3a5a186ca19e99079a4b5c9af479d0" :answer/id #uuid "71da9d86-9793-50ad-bd48-53f7e54f5912" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81474/selection/ca783ed101534bce784086928334be52e41af8a48bb5928cb06b33e258213450" :answer/id #uuid "64ea1d6b-87e4-549e-8533-49aa0fdf4c8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81474/selection/dbc7b884b45f4632f612b1c367e922ff04a1a8cb72bcdd202ce3b9da821f5d79" :answer/id #uuid "8e305e54-abfc-5bff-96e1-5a8ab1c1d05a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "22\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81474/selection/1953051474e7d297116aa5a4bd8aa18eaa02a238250d8d06ecc5b7c1b900ff8a" :answer/id #uuid "21e65870-2b27-5894-a0a0-203908584a4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81474/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c0556b96-5033-5370-8905-0acdcd83681b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81474/selection/65d8c559c809217f473c7ef19de0ff6b5a3a5a186ca19e99079a4b5c9af479d0" :answer-field/choices ["q-81474/selection/41960dd54deb249b69963946aad073a9efdee28d29175fa0fb77c9989bed55c0" "q-81474/selection/65d8c559c809217f473c7ef19de0ff6b5a3a5a186ca19e99079a4b5c9af479d0" "q-81474/selection/ca783ed101534bce784086928334be52e41af8a48bb5928cb06b33e258213450" "q-81474/selection/dbc7b884b45f4632f612b1c367e922ff04a1a8cb72bcdd202ce3b9da821f5d79" "q-81474/selection/1953051474e7d297116aa5a4bd8aa18eaa02a238250d8d06ecc5b7c1b900ff8a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81474" :question/id #uuid "1f8fadaa-0d78-521b-ae7c-e7c1f771ff78" :question/math-academy-id "q-81474" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in $\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=6{t}^{2}-2t-10$, where $t$ is the time in seconds. If the particle has velocity $v=-4\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}$ when $t=1\\,\\text{s}$, calculate the speed of the particle at the moment $t=3\\,\\text{s}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (6{t}^{2}-2t-10)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}-10t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(1)=-4.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4 & =2(1)^{3}-(1)^{2}-10(1)+C \\\\ -4 & =2-1-10+C \\\\ C & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=2{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}-10t+5.$\n\nWe evaluate the velocity at time $t=3\\,\\text{s}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(3) & =2(3)^{3}-(3)^{2}-10(3)+5 \\\\  & =54-9-30+5 \\\\  & =20\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the speed is equal to $|v(t)|,$ we conclude that the speed of the particle is $20\\,\\text{m/s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-81474/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee2920dc-93e1-5595-a751-62ad5e4f3035"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81474"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-351060/field-1/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "8d5488f4-d374-58ea-8bc4-f38768158635" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351060/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "53be91c7-9f20-5aab-8680-c267e0647063" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351060/field-1/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer-field/choices ["q-351060/field-1/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351060" :question/id #uuid "2da25941-d469-57cc-a3a6-d483c3ddfc08" :question/math-academy-id "q-351060" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration $a(t)=-\\frac{4}{(t+1)^{2}},$ where $a(t)$ is measured in ${\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ and $t$ is measured in seconds. Find the speed of the particle at the moment $t=1\\,\\text{s}$ given that the particle has velocity $v=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{m/s}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{s}.$\n\nThe speed at the moment $t=1\\,\\text{s}$ is\n{{field-1}} $\\,\\text{m/s}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int -\\frac{4}{(t+1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{t+1}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(0)=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{4}{0+1}+C \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =4+C \\\\ C & =-\\frac{7}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=\\frac{4}{t+1}-\\frac{7}{2}.$\n\nWe evaluate the velocity at time $t=1\\,\\text{s}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =\\frac{4}{1+1}-\\frac{7}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2}-\\frac{7}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2}-\\frac{7}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the speed is equal to $|v(t)|,$ we conclude that the speed of the particle is $\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\text{m/s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-351060/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f20159e8-8f86-5bf8-b87e-3eb990b819f1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351060"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-102742/selection/4f6906659fea143af1f12a0239c40d6e7b02fa5f703d67f4f681fe25bd0b22c6" :answer/id #uuid "6e747da3-ae63-568a-8c91-04d46faaa91d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102742/selection/45f37bc6a1a07c92b7c904eb728ce4f0c4096ae0848f8c5251e0022341feb628" :answer/id #uuid "8d189dfd-5fc4-5f1a-85b0-9474fffcd654" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102742/selection/3f2a3f03b9d39f29b54117dffa5e88e7ba94e4f7415f9687da9e2695670d56da" :answer/id #uuid "68635bc5-8612-5cca-8be1-80f8a4d3de21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102742/selection/c28f7256c0503cafa07ff7521b86d7026f482ead5c5334daa1c1cea8f1117460" :answer/id #uuid "08cc742c-dd38-51b2-8359-afdcbed46083" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102742/selection/5004d5487e89baff2f9e09fe879f1cac1706413e1118514466ab3b3e8519cb3f" :answer/id #uuid "d478c8eb-c35e-515e-b6b9-06132200075e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102742/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "411ffd2b-061a-59ec-9cf3-f702d8c3d8a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-102742/selection/45f37bc6a1a07c92b7c904eb728ce4f0c4096ae0848f8c5251e0022341feb628" :answer-field/choices ["q-102742/selection/4f6906659fea143af1f12a0239c40d6e7b02fa5f703d67f4f681fe25bd0b22c6" "q-102742/selection/45f37bc6a1a07c92b7c904eb728ce4f0c4096ae0848f8c5251e0022341feb628" "q-102742/selection/3f2a3f03b9d39f29b54117dffa5e88e7ba94e4f7415f9687da9e2695670d56da" "q-102742/selection/c28f7256c0503cafa07ff7521b86d7026f482ead5c5334daa1c1cea8f1117460" "q-102742/selection/5004d5487e89baff2f9e09fe879f1cac1706413e1118514466ab3b3e8519cb3f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102742" :question/id #uuid "1ac29eea-5742-54dd-bfcd-cbd57bf8e08c" :question/math-academy-id "q-102742" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration $a(t)=\\sqrt{{t}^{3}},$ where $a(t)$ is measured in ${\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ and $t$ is measured in seconds. If the particle has velocity $v=0\\,\\text{m/s}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{s}$, calculate the speed of the particle at the moment $t=1\\,\\text{s}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \\sqrt{{t}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int {t}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}{t}^{5/2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(0)=0.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =\\frac{2}{5}(0)^{5/2}+C \\\\ 0 & =0+C \\\\ C & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=\\frac{2}{5}{t}^{5/2}.$\n\nWe evaluate the velocity at time $t=1\\,\\text{s}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =\\frac{2}{5}(1)^{5/2}=\\frac{2}{5}\\,\\text{m/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the speed is equal to $|v(t)|,$ we conclude that the speed of the particle is $\\frac{2}{5}\\,\\text{m/s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-102742/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f20159e8-8f86-5bf8-b87e-3eb990b819f1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102742"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-19487/selection/61dff08a1a28bd69c5c76d39187a3bfff29da82b7a520d0fb04c2d44fb2324e5" :answer/id #uuid "12366a0f-3ccf-575e-8a83-12fee14f805b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.33\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19487/selection/eb8851fb46e7eddb12eef2e96575478158560459f245a7b388cdc73552332252" :answer/id #uuid "b92273d9-ab8e-5ecb-9f15-bb56758d7924" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.75\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19487/selection/8a3b70cd8f25f1cfd43c1136bea896132d1f3cb4090e1351b9bd27c32bfacc94" :answer/id #uuid "8622f8bd-e5c3-5c92-9ede-f40b3f102e71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.25\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19487/selection/93f1692da4721f92f3e92adfd753c823600d583a9239484de60b1355b478a8e5" :answer/id #uuid "f0656c44-8d51-5fb2-bb3c-6a76fa1f8b79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.75\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19487/selection/a0475d7965b797499d35571ccb3c95bc801c56a503a0cb334aee0b2e597529db" :answer/id #uuid "88f59713-2416-5173-be6f-cefdba3b6416" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19487/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e52358ec-5418-582d-84ec-876052a9389f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-19487/selection/93f1692da4721f92f3e92adfd753c823600d583a9239484de60b1355b478a8e5" :answer-field/choices ["q-19487/selection/61dff08a1a28bd69c5c76d39187a3bfff29da82b7a520d0fb04c2d44fb2324e5" "q-19487/selection/eb8851fb46e7eddb12eef2e96575478158560459f245a7b388cdc73552332252" "q-19487/selection/8a3b70cd8f25f1cfd43c1136bea896132d1f3cb4090e1351b9bd27c32bfacc94" "q-19487/selection/93f1692da4721f92f3e92adfd753c823600d583a9239484de60b1355b478a8e5" "q-19487/selection/a0475d7965b797499d35571ccb3c95bc801c56a503a0cb334aee0b2e597529db"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-19487" :question/id #uuid "1e694ce3-05d1-58d3-bfbc-b58138322825" :question/math-academy-id "q-19487" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in $\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)$, where $t$ is the time in seconds. If the particle has velocity $v=0\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}$ when $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,\\text{s}$, find the velocity of the particle at time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\,\\text{s}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t))\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t))+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=0.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})+C \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )+C \\\\ C & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t).$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the velocity at time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\,\\text{s}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =0.75\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-19487/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f20159e8-8f86-5bf8-b87e-3eb990b819f1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-19487"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81710/selection/47419b058768c7a8b9952e20a998e23ba848a472aa19e8afbf5c613fca599a62" :answer/id #uuid "cecfbe4f-d6cd-574b-a887-60c20f75af65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,\\text{ft}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81710/selection/9f08d6586b397302880e8e44a93b69d805e3e579c76300e1b31babec134a3eba" :answer/id #uuid "eda28035-baf7-523a-9638-4173ed32875f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,\\text{ft}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81710/selection/d00c939e4b43a2fe0d65bc30043166d8be3b57fd27885d4817ff0f7870fb67e9" :answer/id #uuid "43ddfe83-f8d4-52b4-8ce5-6ca02300c4a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,\\text{ft}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81710/selection/6f7892bd3c14f9295c037645846f5f11b0c8182a214e108d3a7a589d4e6dadfa" :answer/id #uuid "1614ac07-63ff-5d36-8b64-acacbcb5c27b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\,\\text{ft}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81710/selection/ddc24a81fd6dcd95c0e475c7a3a5436323ffe4d610f9098292ed0036d76ffc8b" :answer/id #uuid "540c8d32-1691-5eb9-9022-655ecc1644b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\,\\text{ft}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81710/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "62cdb047-288d-5b95-82e5-eb922356d91f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81710/selection/6f7892bd3c14f9295c037645846f5f11b0c8182a214e108d3a7a589d4e6dadfa" :answer-field/choices ["q-81710/selection/47419b058768c7a8b9952e20a998e23ba848a472aa19e8afbf5c613fca599a62" "q-81710/selection/9f08d6586b397302880e8e44a93b69d805e3e579c76300e1b31babec134a3eba" "q-81710/selection/d00c939e4b43a2fe0d65bc30043166d8be3b57fd27885d4817ff0f7870fb67e9" "q-81710/selection/6f7892bd3c14f9295c037645846f5f11b0c8182a214e108d3a7a589d4e6dadfa" "q-81710/selection/ddc24a81fd6dcd95c0e475c7a3a5436323ffe4d610f9098292ed0036d76ffc8b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81710" :question/id #uuid "733f11d7-9615-5c7c-9d3b-78f5e942f1ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-81710" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in $\\text{ft}/{\\text{s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)$, where $t$ is the time in seconds. If the particle has velocity $v=3\\,\\text{ft}/\\text{s}$ when $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\,\\text{s}$, calculate the speed of the particle at the moment $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,\\text{s}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t))+C \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=3.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})+C \\\\ 3 & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+C \\\\ 3 & =-2\\cdot 0+C \\\\ C & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=3-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t).$\n\nWe evaluate the velocity at time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,\\text{s}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =3-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =3-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ) \\\\  & =3-2\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =5\\,\\text{ft}/\\text{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the speed is equal to $|v(t)|,$ we conclude that the speed of the particle is $5\\,\\text{ft}/\\text{s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-81710/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f20159e8-8f86-5bf8-b87e-3eb990b819f1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81710"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81709/selection/f344b25ecabf672e424f034f7c7c97eb9866d569aecc3a9650dd3a23dd2dee90" :answer/id #uuid "6fa1e3ed-9b96-5706-8a7a-7d6ae8f03a7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(t)=4-3{e}^{-2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81709/selection/e8fa356e2029fe3fe3b304fe275487a4ee60b3881738c17d1d30bf1c9a4c5677" :answer/id #uuid "48e012c2-aa4f-5fcc-88b1-453915e7d7fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(t)=4{e}^{-t}-27{e}^{-3t}+24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81709/selection/2eb3e17b601217b5f1652701fc7920572d6d916c00a436a41336579fbc6b9048" :answer/id #uuid "83777860-0064-5ae2-b5e5-0be5d41c2b7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(t)=4{e}^{-2t}-27{e}^{-4t}+24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81709/selection/a9e0f77ee1f068fd0a6574e4f21185b357157e2cdff126f7b6997b48dbc78dfb" :answer/id #uuid "85c30624-87ef-5db2-acd3-2cea9071754d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(t)=4{e}^{-t}-3{e}^{-3t}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81709/selection/6131c92aa4c6b701713c4674963d1020d0280a400a81170f8bb2dd07fb2448cc" :answer/id #uuid "ec81c54e-b22b-59b5-98e9-0508a7728308" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(t)=4{e}^{-t}-3{e}^{-3t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81709/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bfd6d054-fece-5ffd-a711-5d40a53dfbc4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81709/selection/6131c92aa4c6b701713c4674963d1020d0280a400a81170f8bb2dd07fb2448cc" :answer-field/choices ["q-81709/selection/f344b25ecabf672e424f034f7c7c97eb9866d569aecc3a9650dd3a23dd2dee90" "q-81709/selection/e8fa356e2029fe3fe3b304fe275487a4ee60b3881738c17d1d30bf1c9a4c5677" "q-81709/selection/2eb3e17b601217b5f1652701fc7920572d6d916c00a436a41336579fbc6b9048" "q-81709/selection/a9e0f77ee1f068fd0a6574e4f21185b357157e2cdff126f7b6997b48dbc78dfb" "q-81709/selection/6131c92aa4c6b701713c4674963d1020d0280a400a81170f8bb2dd07fb2448cc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81709" :question/id #uuid "adaf0a1a-e89f-5330-af89-83ce6c6e01c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-81709" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in $\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=9{e}^{-3t}-4{e}^{-t}$, where $t$ is the time in seconds. If the particle has velocity $v=1\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{s}$, find the velocity (in $\\text{m/s}$)  of the particle at time $t.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (9{e}^{-3t}-4{e}^{-t})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =9(-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-3t})-4(-{e}^{-t})+C \\\\  & =-3{e}^{-3t}+4{e}^{-t}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(0)=1.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =-3{e}^{0}+4{e}^{0}+C \\\\ 1 & =-3+4+C \\\\ C & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=4{e}^{-t}-3{e}^{-3t}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-81709/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f20159e8-8f86-5bf8-b87e-3eb990b819f1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81709"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-562"] :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in $\\textrm m / \\textrm s^2,$ given by the function $a(t) = 4t^2 - 3t^3,$ where $t$ is the time in seconds. If the particle has velocity $v=2\\,\\textrm m / \\textrm s$ when $t=0 \\,\\textrm s,$ calculate the velocity (in $\\textrm m / \\textrm s$) of the particle at time $t.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (4{t}^{2}-3{t}^{3})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{t}^{3}-\\frac{3}{4}{t}^{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C,$ we use the fact that $v(0) = 2.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =\\frac{4}{3}(0)^{3}-\\frac{3}{4}(0)^{4}+C \\\\ C & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t) = \\dfrac{4}{3}t^3 -\\dfrac{3}{4}t^4 + 2.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-563"] :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in $\\textrm m / \\textrm s^2,$ given by the function $a(t) =2e^{-t}+6t^2$, where $t$ is the time in seconds. If the particle has velocity $v=-4 \\,\\textrm m / \\textrm s$ when $t=0 \\,\\textrm s,$ calculate the speed of the particle at the moment  $t=1\\,\\textrm{s}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (2{e}^{-t}+6{t}^{2})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2(-{e}^{-t})+\\frac{6}{3}{t}^{3}+C \\\\  & =-2{e}^{-t}+2{t}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(0) = -4.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4 & =-2{e}^{-0}+2\\cdot {0}^{3}+C \\\\ -4 & =-2+0+C \\\\ C & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t) = -2  e^{-t}+ 2t^3 -2.$\n\nWe evaluate the velocity at time $t=1\\,\\textrm{s}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =-2{e}^{-1}+2(1)^{3}-2 \\\\  & =-2{e}^{-1}+2-2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{e}\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the speed is equal to $|v(t)|,$ we conclude that the speed of the particle is $\\dfrac 2 e\\,\\textrm{m/s}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
